Explanation of the two changes:

- We un‐comment the `hints.nested` guard so that nested lane deletions also rerun the compensation routine.
- We insert a new branch at the top of `compensateLaneDelete` that, when the deleted lane was the last child, programmatically “collapses” its parent by resizing it upward by the deleted lane’s height. This prevents the orphaned empty parent lane from leaving a gap in the diagram.
